The SQL parser under src/ (the ast/, dialect/, parser/ trees plus tokenizer.rs,
keywords.rs, display_utils.rs, test_utils.rs, and the crate scaffolding in
lib.rs) is an in-tree hard fork of Apache DataFusion's sqlparser-rs.

  project: https://github.com/apache/datafusion-sqlparser-rs
  tag:     v0.62.0
  commit:  3dd0e30d8bb1d2a6775f62d2b84839b60133effb

Fork point is a near-verbatim copy of the tag's src/ (upstream's tests/, derive/,
and examples/ were not vendored; the sqlparser_derive proc-macro is left as an
unused optional dependency). CrabgreSQL-specific additions live in later commits;
diffing src/ against this tag shows our divergence. Re-sync by replacing src/
from a newer tag and updating the commit above.

Deliberate divergences from upstream (things a re-sync must re-apply, not
discard):

  * OperateFunctionArg gained `data_type_span`, so CREATE FUNCTION can point a
    caret at an argument type in the "type is only a shell" NOTICE.
  * New `Statement::Do` / `DoStatement`. Upstream has no DO statement at all.
  * `parse_routine_body_literal` factored out of
    `parse_create_function_body_string`, so CREATE FUNCTION, CREATE PROCEDURE
    and DO share one body-literal path and all keep the literal's span.
  * `Statement::CreateProcedure` reshaped from upstream's T-SQL grammar
    (`LANGUAGE x AS <statement list> END`, unreachable from the PG dialect) to
    PostgreSQL's (`(args) LANGUAGE x AS $$...$$`), as a `CreateProcedure`
    struct. The attribute-clause loop is shared with CREATE FUNCTION via
    `parse_pg_routine_options`, mirroring PG's single `createfunc_opt_list`
    production. `ProcedureParam`, `parse_optional_procedure_parameters` and
    `parse_procedure_param` were removed as dead — procedures now use
    `parse_function_arg`/`OperateFunctionArg`.
  * The `CREATE PROCEDURE` dispatch moved above the `or_replace` bail in
    `parse_create`, so `CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE` parses.
